   "title": "Jensen Huang vs. Steve Jobs: Can Nvidia also thrive without its visionary?",
   "description": "<p>Longtime Nvidia (<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" class=\"link\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/NVDA/\" data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\">NVDA</a>) CEO Jensen Huang has resigned as chief executive following a string of personal controversies.</p>\n<p>Yahoo Finance's Julie Hyman chats with SoFi (<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" class=\"link\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/SOFI/\" data-i13n=\"slk:SOFI;cpos:2;pos:1\">SOFI</a>) chief market strategist Liz Thomas and Moor Insights & Strategy founder Patrick Moorhead at Yahoo Finance's 2026 Invest conference to discuss the parallels between Steve Jobs for Apple (<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" class=\"link\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AAPL/\" data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\">AAPL</a>) and Huang for Nvidia.</p>\n<p></p>",
   "summary": "Longtime Nvidia (NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang has resigned as chief executive following a string of personal controversies.\n\nYahoo Finance's Julie Hyman chats with SoFi (SOFI) chief market strategist Liz Thomas and Moor Insights &amp; Strategy founder Patrick Moorhead at Yahoo Finance's 2026 Invest conference to discuss the parallels between Steve Jobs for Apple (AAPL) and Huang for Nvidia.\n\n",
